#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0165 expect=noViolation domain=ADLB
#note "Non-firing counterpart: 001/HGB/PRE keeps the filter-discriminating pair (post-baseline ATOXGR 'GRADE 3' above baseline 'GRADE 2', BTOXGR='GRADE 2' everywhere - a filter-ignoring max() would false-fire and red this scenario) and 003 keeps only the empty-BTOXGR no-baseline row, held quiet by the non_empty guard. An inverted equality (firing on BTOXGR == baseline ATOXGR) fires on rows 1-2 and reds this too."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLB label="Analysis Dataset Lab"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PARAMCD  type=Char label="Parameter Code"
col BASETYPE type=Char label="Baseline Type"
col AVISITN  type=Num  label="Analysis Visit (N)"
col ABLFL    type=Char label="Baseline Record Flag"
col ATOXGR   type=Char label="Analysis Toxicity Grade"
col BTOXGR   type=Char label="Baseline Toxicity Grade"
---
S1 | 001 | HGB | PRE | 0 | Y | GRADE 2 | GRADE 2
S1 | 001 | HGB | PRE | 1 |   | GRADE 3 | GRADE 2
S1 | 003 | HGB | PRE | 2 |   | GRADE 1 |
